# OpenRouter model picker

This project previously used a `beforeSubmitPrompt` hook to block every Agent
send until one of a fixed set of OpenRouter models was selected. That hook has
been removed (2026-09-26) — Cursor did not reliably pass the selected model
into the hook payload, so it always saw "unknown" and blocked all prompts,
including ones with the intended bypass prefix.

The favorite models are still listed in `.cursor/openrouter-models.json` and
used by `.cursor/or-ask.mjs` for one-off terminal calls to OpenRouter:

1. `stealth/space-bunny-alpha` — Space Bunny Alpha
2. `nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free` — Nemotron 3 Ultra (free)
3. `inclusionai/ling-3.0-flash-fin:free` — Ling 3.0 Flash Fin (free)
4. `z-ai/glm-5.3-flash` — GLM 5.3 Flash (paid)

If the user asks to call OpenRouter MCP, confirm the slug before
`send-message`, but do not block or gate the request on it.

Never put `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` in repo files, commits, or chat logs.
